{"name":"Apple II Chocolate","hex":"#da680e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"apple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common, firm, round fruit produced by a tree of the genus Malus.","The fruit of the tree Malus domestica, chiefly with a green, red, or yellow skin, cultivated in temperate climates for cidermaking, cooking, and eating. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (something) appear like an apple (noun sense 1.1).","To become like an apple.\n\n To collect fir-cones.\n Of a flower bud or vegetable (especially a root vegetable): to grow into the shape of an apple."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apple"},{"term":"chocolate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food made from ground roasted cocoa beans.","A drink made by dissolving this food in boiling milk or water."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of or containing chocolate.","Having a dark reddish-brown colour/color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chocolate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Apple II","blocks":[{"text":"The Apple II is a series of microcomputers manufactured by Apple Computer, Inc. from 1977 to 1993. The original Apple II model, which gave the series its name, was designed by Steve Wozniak and was first sold on June 10, 1977. Its success led to the Apple II Plus, Apple IIe, Apple IIc, and Apple IIc Plus, with the IIe being the most popular. The name is trademarked with square brackets as apple ][, then beginning with the IIe in 1983 as Apple //."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Apple_II-IMG_7064.jpg/330px-Apple_II-IMG_7064.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_II","wikidata":"Q201652"},{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple","wikidata":"Q89"},{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate","wikidata":"Q195"},{"title":"Chocolate (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color chocolate or cocoa brown is a shade of brown that resembles chocolate. At right is displayed the color traditionally called chocolate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Chocolate02.jpg/330px-Chocolate02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate_(color)","wikidata":"Q3309916"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Apple_iie.jpg/500px-Apple_iie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Apple_iie.jpg/500px-Apple_iie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Apple IIe with DuoDisk and Monitor //","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AApple_iie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimed